.Sh BUGS
The in-kernel NAT facilities based on
.Xr libalias 3 ,
that is the
.Cm nat
action of
.Xr ipfw 8
and
.Xr ng_nat 4 ,
do not repair delayed transmit checksums on packets received from
another interface: their repair logic assumes that a packet with a
pending checksum was generated locally.
Traffic forwarded from an
.Nm
interface with transmit checksum offloading enabled is therefore
emitted with invalid TCP and UDP checksums after passing through such
NAT.
.Xr epair 4
is affected in the same way.
.Xr natd 8
operating on a
.Xr divert 4
socket is not affected: diverted packets have their checksums
completed before they reach the socket.
As a workaround, disable transmit checksum offloading on the pair:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
ifconfig pair0a -txcsum -txcsum6
.Ed
